5. Run repeated nested five-fold cross-validation for both models and baselines.
6. Tune regularization and boosting complexity only within training folds.
7. Evaluate log-MAE, USD-MAE, RMSE, and median absolute percentage error; emphasize MAE because percentage metrics can distort low-priced boats.
8. Produce calibration plots, residual diagnostics, subgroup errors, partial-effect plots, and prediction intervals.
9. Freeze parameters, rerun once on the prescribed split, and record outputs.

